  "course": {
    "narrative": "An 87-year-old female was admitted following a hip fracture and subsequent T9 and T8 thoracic compression fractures treated with vertebroplasty. She reported significant mid-to-lower back pain, as well as new depressive symptoms including loss of interest, crying spells, decreased appetite, and passive suicidal thoughts (noting she did not mind dying). She denied active suicidal or homicidal ideations, hallucinations, or manic symptoms. On mental status examination, she was alert and oriented x3 with fair memory and judgment, and scored 28/30 on the MMSE. She was diagnosed with major depressive disorder. The treatment plan includes continuing Lexapro and Pamelor while monitoring for adverse effects and worsening depression, along with discussions regarding potential inpatient psychiatric care.",
